"""The load-time banner: "Money Follows My Brother", as coloured ASCII.

Purely decorative and deliberately harmless: `show()` swallows everything, so a terminal
that dislikes it cannot stop the pack loading.

HOW IT WAS MADE - the art is BAKED, never derived at runtime, and the screenshot is not
a dependency. The subject was cut out with cv2 GrabCut, because his face and the studio
background share a luminance median (96 against 79) and no amount of contrast tuning
separates them - the first attempts produced a wall of noise with a hole where the face
should be. The subject's own tonal range was then stretched, local contrast applied
inside the matte only, and the result mapped onto a 23-step character ramp with per-cell
24-bit colour. Bright background props keep a little presence, so the mic and the
trophies still read.

The captions are real Roboto-Black glyphs from this pack's own fonts/ folder, rasterised
to the 96-column grid at two scanlines per row via the half-block characters. At one
scanline per row "Money Follows" rasterised as "Monoy Followe".

It prints in ONE write. Not a micro-optimisation: ComfyUI-Manager wraps stdout with a
lock and wandb patches it again, and this install has already lost a run to those
contending inside an ordinary print(). Forty-five separate writes at startup is the
shape of that problem; one is not.

Turn it off with  ARK_BANNER=0  in the environment.
"""

